DATA SOURCES
------------

Raw downloads are gitignored (`data/raw/`) and re-fetched on first run. What is
committed under `data/processed/` and `docs/players.js` is transformed output —
model coefficients, ratings and valuations — not reproduced source tables. It is
included so results can be inspected without re-running the pipeline. None of it
is relicensed by this project's MIT license, and it should not be treated as a
redistribution of the underlying datasets.

  wehoop / SportsDataverse — MIT licensed
    https://github.com/sportsdataverse/wehoop
    Box scores, play-by-play, rosters, player metadata, and the archived
    WNBA Stats possession/lineup data.

  Basketball-Reference (Sports Reference LLC)
    https://www.basketball-reference.com/
    NBA and WNBA advanced statistics and WNBA draft history, used to fit the
    box-score prior. Accessed at their requested rate limit. Their terms
    restrict bulk redistribution; only fitted coefficients and derived ratings
    are committed here, never their tables.

  Her Hoop Stats
    https://herhoopstats.com/
    2026 WNBA salary and contract data.

  ESPN
    Play-by-play and rosters, reached via the wehoop mirrors above.


METHOD AND PRIOR ART
--------------------

Not licensing obligations, but this project would not exist without them.

  412 Sports Analytics — the rating method: a transfer-learned box-score prior,
    possession-level RAPM, and a ridge that shrinks toward the prior rather than
    toward zero.
    https://412sportsanalytics.wordpress.com/2022/08/18/a-detailed-guide-for-developing-player-ratings-for-wnba-and-other-leagues/

  Stephen Noh, nbasalarymodel — the template for turning a player rating into a
    contract valuation, and for the shape of this site.
    https://github.com/StephenNoh/nbasalarymodel

  Seth Partnow, "The Midrange Theory" — the rating to wins to dollars chain.

  Kostya Medvedovsky, DARKO — the reference point for a predictive player-impact
    system. https://www.darko.app/

  sportsdataverse-py — the bundled WNBA aging curve used for projections.
